# Redirect all non-www traffic to www permanently
#
# NOTE: this rule is currently NOT what is serving the apex redirect in
# production. https://supplyministry.com.au/ answers with a 302 (verified
# 2026-08-08) despite the forced 301 below, and the response carries
# `server: cloudflare`. The redirect is therefore being applied at the
# Cloudflare edge, ahead of this file. Changing the status code to 301 has to
# be done in the Cloudflare dashboard (Rules -> Redirect Rules); editing this
# line alone will not do it.
https://supplyministry.com.au/* https://www.supplyministry.com.au/:splat 301!

# Dynamic sitemap served from the Supabase edge function.
#
# This rewrite was previously shadowed by a physical public/sitemap.xml, which
# static hosts serve in preference to a non-forced rewrite. That is why the live
# sitemap only ever showed six hand-written URLs. The static file has been
# removed and the rule is now forced, so the edge function actually answers.
/sitemap.xml https://yngbsrovafbnczjaybkc.supabase.co/functions/v1/sitemap 200!
